# Supabase

Jachai uses Supabase for **auth**, **Pro entitlement**, **user research metadata**, and **planned bKash checkout** — not for articles/clusters or verified claims (those live in backend PostgreSQL).

## Layout

- `supabase/config.toml` — local CLI project (`project_id = "jachai-news"`, Postgres 15)
- `supabase/migrations/` — versioned SQL:
  - `20250301000000_init_profiles_subscriptions.sql` — profiles, subscriptions, bKash tables
  - `20250302000000_security_rls_hardening.sql` — `saved_dossiers`, `custom_alerts`, explicit deny INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on billing tables for anon/authenticated
- Frontend types: `frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts` — **keep in sync** when migrations change

## Apply schema

- Linked project: `supabase db push`
- Or paste migration SQL into the Supabase dashboard SQL editor
- Local dev: `supabase start` then `supabase db reset` / push as needed

Regenerate TS types after schema changes:

```bash
npx supabase gen types typescript --local > frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts
```

(Use `--project-id` for remote when not using local.)

## Tables & enums

| Object | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `public.profiles` | One row per `auth.users`; `locale` `en` \| `bn`; auto-created via `handle_new_user` trigger |
| `public.subscriptions` | One row per user (`user_id` unique); `subscription_plan` monthly/yearly; `subscription_status` trialing/active/past_due/canceled/expired |
| `public.bkash_agreements` | Tokenized checkout agreement IDs per user (planned) |
| `public.payment_transactions` | bKash (default provider) charges linked to `subscription_id`; `metadata` jsonb |
| `public.saved_dossiers` | Per-user research notes + source URLs (full CRUD for owner) |
| `public.custom_alerts` | Per-user saved search/alert queries (full CRUD for owner) |

## Row Level Security

- RLS enabled on all public tables above
- **Profiles**: users SELECT/UPDATE own row
- **Subscriptions / bKash / payments**: users SELECT own rows only; **no client INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE** (explicit deny policies in hardening migration) — writes for **service role** only
- **Dossiers / alerts**: users full CRUD on own rows (`auth.uid() = user_id`)
- Never use `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` for subscription writes or admin bootstrap; use server routes with `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`

## Frontend wiring

- **Clients**: `lib/supabase/client.ts` (browser), `server.ts` (cookie session in RSC/routes), `service.ts` (service role, server-only), `config.ts` (`isSupabaseConfigured`); re-exported from `lib/supabase.ts`
- Session refresh: `lib/supabase/middleware.ts` from root `middleware.ts` (browse + auth paths + `sb-*` cookies)
- Admin bootstrap: `POST /api/admin/register` sets `app_metadata.role=admin` when registration code + service role are configured
- **Admin Users tab** (`lib/admin-users.ts`, server-only): `auth.admin.listUsers` / create / delete; reads `profiles` + `subscriptions`; **`setAdminUserPlan`** upserts active `subscriptions` rows for manual Pro grants — never expose service role to the browser (proxies under `/api/admin/users*` with legacy admin cookie)
- **Pro entitlements**: server `getProAccessState()` in `subscription-access.ts` SELECTs own `subscriptions` row (RLS); `subscription-entitlement.ts` implements `isActiveProSubscription`; type helper `SubscriptionEntitlementRow` in `database.types.ts`. Override locally with `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO=true`
- Pricing/feature copy stays in `subscription-plans.ts` and `subscription-features.ts` (not in DB)

## Migrations conventions

- One logical change per migration file; timestamp prefix `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_name.sql`
- Prefer explicit RLS policies and comments on tables intended for service-role writes
- Do not store news/RSS/cluster/verification data here; do not commit service role keys or bKash secrets
